              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ingenuus, ingenua, ingenuum — \"free-born; frank\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hic puer ingenuus est, nōn servus. This boy is free-born, not a slave."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Born free, as against lībertīnus; then honest, frank. English ingenuous."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ingenuus is built on in- and the root of gignō \"to beget\" (Lewis & Short): born in the place, then born free. English ingenuous comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
